ommunication issues are severe enough to jeopardize crew safety, would lead me to reconsider.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}", "thoughts": "We have gathered info from others: Agent1 and Agent2 both said they lack info on D technical and A stress. So we have our own info: we have the full list of attributes for all candidates. Let's list them:\n\nCandidate A: can anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Also unfriendly, eats unhealthily.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills. Also regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone when communicating.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nWe need to evaluate for long-distance pilot: reliability/responsibility, technical/cognitive competence, calmness/judgment under pressure, decision-making, teamwork/communication, professional development.\n\nLet's assess each:\n\nA: Anticipate dangerous situations (good for safety), see complex connections (cognitive), excellent spatial vision (important for navigation), very good leadership (crew cooperation). Weaknesses: unfriendly (teamwork), eats unhealthily (could affect long flights health). No info on stress handling, decision speed, communication style. Leadership good but unfriendly may hinder crew. Overall strong technical but teamwork concerns.\n\nB: Very conscientious (reliability), handles stress very well (calm under pressure), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (navigation